  norm(m,'The Nimbus 365 Coupé is a Swedish all-weather family cruiser built around an enclosed deck saloon, two cabins and shaft-drive diesel propulsion. Factory documentation shows both single- and twin-engine options, making exact machinery configuration important when comparing individual boats.',['Excellent enclosed visibility and weather protection','Two-cabin layout supports extended couple or family cruising','Factory shaft-drive diesel choices avoid sterndrive dependence'],['Systems and accommodation are more complex than a compact single-cabin cruiser','Twin-engine examples increase maintenance burden and machinery-space crowding','Higher cruising speeds carry greater fuel use than displacement trawlers'],['Couples or families wanting an all-weather Scandinavian cruiser','Extended inland and coastal cruising','Owners prioritizing enclosed helm comfort and practical side access'],['You require a narrow trailerable boat','You want minimal systems and single-purpose simplicity','You primarily want 6–7-knot displacement economy'],['Confirm single- or twin-engine factory configuration','Inspect shaft seals, stern gear, cooling and exhaust systems','Inspect deck saloon windows, doors and roof openings for leakage','Review electrical, heating, hot-water and sanitation systems','Verify air draft with mast and antenna configuration'],[{'Name':'Engine alternatives','Description':'Factory specifications document both single D6 and twin D4 shaft-drive configurations with materially different weight and performance.','AffectedYears':'Production run','EvidenceRefs':S['Nimbus365'],'Confidence':'High'}],S['Nimbus365'])

